description:
# DiscordBridge

A [PowerNukkitX](https://github.com/PowerNukkitX/PowerNukkitX) plugin that connects your Minecraft server to a Discord bot.

---

## Requirements

- PowerNukkitX (nightly build or compatible release)
- Java 21+
- A Discord bot token from the [Discord Developer Portal](https://discord.com/developers/applications)

---

## Installation

1. Download the latest release.
2. Drop the it into your PNX server's `plugins/` folder.

3. Start the server once to generate `plugins/DiscordBridge/config.yml`, then stop it.

4. Open `config.yml` and paste your bot token:
   ```yaml
   bot-token: "YOUR_BOT_TOKEN_HERE"
   ```

5. Start the server again. If the token is valid you'll see:
   ```
   [DiscordBridge] Connected to Discord as YourBotName#1234
   ```

---

## Configuration

```yaml
# Discord bot token from the Developer Portal.
bot-token: "REPLACE_ME"

# Rate limiting — applied per plugin that uses the API.
rate-limit:
  max-actions: 20      # max requests allowed per window
  window-seconds: 10   # how long the window lasts

# Print all incoming Discord messages to console.
debug-logging: false
```

The rate limiter runs per plugin name, so if one plugin hits the limit it won't block others.

---

## Using DiscordBridge in your Plugin

First, add DiscordBridge as a dependency in your plugin's `plugin.yml`:

```yaml
depend: ["DiscordBridge"]
```

Then grab the `Bot` instance from PNX's service manager:

```java
Bot bot = getServer().getServiceManager()
    .getProvider(Bot.class)
    .getProvider();
```

> Always check `bot.isReady()` before making calls. The bot connects asynchronously on startup, so it may not be ready immediately.

---

## Sending Messages

Send a plain text message to a Discord channel:

```java
// Fire and forget
bot.getMessageManager().sendMessage("123456789012345678", "Server is starting up!", this);

// Wait for the result
bot.getMessageManager().sendMessageAsync("123456789012345678", "Hello from Minecraft!", this)
    .thenAccept(msg -> getLogger().info("Sent message ID: " + msg.getId()))
    .exceptionally(err -> { getLogger().warning("Failed: " + err.getMessage()); return null; });
```

---

## Sending Embeds

Build a rich embed using the `Embed.builder()`:

```java
Embed embed = Embed.builder()
    .title("Player Joined")
    .description("**Steve** just logged in!")
    .color(Color.GREEN)
    .field("World", "Overworld", true)
    .field("Players Online", "12 / 20", true)
    .footer("MyServer • " + LocalDate.now())
    .build();

bot.getMessageManager().sendEmbed("123456789012345678", embed, this);
```

Fields can be inline (side-by-side) or block (full width). Max 25 fields per embed.

---

## Slash Commands

### Registering a command

```java
List<Option> options = List.of(
    Option.required(OptionType.STRING, "player", "Player name to look up"),
    Option.optional(OptionType.BOOLEAN, "detailed", "Show full stats")
);

// Guild command (shows up immediately, only in that server)
bot.getCommandManager().createGuildCommand("123456789012345678", "stats", "Look up a player", options, this);

// Global command (takes up to an hour to appear in all servers)
bot.getCommandManager().createGlobalCommand("ping", "Check if the bot is alive", List.of(), this);
```

### Handling a command

```java
bot.getCommandManager().registerSlashCommandHandler("stats", ctx -> {
    String playerName = ctx.getStringOption("player", "unknown");
    boolean detailed = ctx.getOption("detailed")
        .map(OptionMapping::getAsBoolean)
        .orElse(false);

    if (detailed) {
        ctx.replyEphemeral("Detailed stats for " + playerName + ": ...");
    } else {
        ctx.reply("Stats for " + playerName + ": 100 kills, 5 deaths");
    }
}, this);
```

`replyEphemeral` sends a response only the user who ran the command can see. `reply` sends it publicly.

---

## Listening to Incoming Discord Messages

Register a handler on a specific channel ID. Every message sent to that channel will trigger your callback:

```java
bot.getMessageManager().registerMessageHandler("123456789012345678", ctx -> {
    String name = ctx.getAuthorName();
    String text = ctx.getContent();

    // Relay to Minecraft chat
    getServer().broadcastMessage("[Discord] " + name + ": " + text);

    // Auto-reply to a keyword
    if (text.equalsIgnoreCase("!online")) {
        ctx.reply("Players online: " + getServer().getOnlinePlayers().size());
    }
}, this);
```

---

## Guild & Moderation

```java
Guilds guilds = bot.getGuildManager();

// Kick a user
guilds.kickUser("USER_ID", "GUILD_ID", "Breaking rules", this)
    .thenRun(() -> getLogger().info("Kicked successfully"));

// Ban a user and delete their last 3 days of messages
guilds.banUser("USER_ID", "GUILD_ID", "Spamming", 3, this);

// Unban
guilds.unbanUser("USER_ID", "GUILD_ID", this);

// Check permission level (OWNER, ADMIN, MODERATOR, or USER)
Level level = guilds.getPermissionLevel("USER_ID", "GUILD_ID");
if (level == Level.ADMIN || level == Level.OWNER) {
    // allow sensitive action
}
```

`getPermissionLevel` uses the member cache (no extra API call). Use `getPermissionLevelAsync` if the member might not be cached.

---

## User Management

```java
Users users = bot.getUserManager();

// Change a member's nickname
users.changeNickname("USER_ID", "GUILD_ID", "CoolNewName", this);

// Add or remove a role
users.addRole("USER_ID", "GUILD_ID", "ROLE_ID", this);
users.removeRole("USER_ID", "GUILD_ID", "ROLE_ID", this);
```

---

## Bot Status & Activity

```java
Status status = bot.getStatusManager();

// Show what the bot is "playing"
status.setActivity("Minecraft 1.21");

// Change online status: "online", "idle", "dnd", "invisible"
status.setStatus("idle");

// Clear the activity
status.setActivity(null);
```

---

## PNX Event: MsgEvent

If you'd rather listen via PNX's event system instead of registering a handler directly, `MsgEvent` is fired for every Discord message the bot receives:

```java
@EventHandler
public void onDiscordMessage(MsgEvent event) {
    getLogger().info("[Discord #" + event.getChannelId() + "] " + event.getAuthorName() + ": " + event.getContent());
}
```

Register your listener as usual with `getServer().getPluginManager().registerEvents(this, this)`.

---

## Finding IDs

To get a channel, guild, user, or role ID in Discord: go to Settings → Advanced → enable **Developer Mode**. Then right-click any server, channel, user, or role and click **Copy ID**.

---

## Notes

- Messages are automatically sanitized — `@everyone` and `@here` pings are blocked, Minecraft color codes (`§a`, `§b`, etc.) are stripped, and messages over 2000 characters are truncated.
- All IDs (user, guild, channel, role) are validated as Discord snowflakes. Passing a non-numeric or wrong-length ID will throw an `IllegalArgumentException` immediately.
- The bot shuts down cleanly when the server stops — it waits up to 5 seconds for in-flight requests before force-closing.
